Description: Don't decline a repeated ADDBA request when the driver reorders frames
 When a peer sends an ADDBA Request with the dialog token of a receive Block
 Ack session that is already set up, mac80211 treats it as an update and
 answers success only if the stored session has the same timeout. Drivers
 that do their own reordering (SUPPORTS_REORDERING_BUFFER, e.g. iwlmvm on
 the AX210) have no tid_rx for that check, so the answer is always "request
 declined". An AP that lost its side of the session and asks again with the
 same token is then refused every time; some APs keep retrying with the
 same token indefinitely and leave the session (and its aggregation) down.
 On those drivers, restart the session as for a request with a new token.
 See docs/DECISIONS.md D9.
Forwarded: no (to be sent to linux-wireless@vger.kernel.org)
Last-Update: 2026-10-06
---
--- a/net/mac80211/agg-rx.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/agg-rx.c
@@ -370,7 +370,14 @@
 	       buf_size, sta->sta.addr);
 
 	if (test_bit(tid, sta->ampdu_mlme.agg_session_valid)) {
-		if (sta->ampdu_mlme.tid_rx_token[tid] == dialog_token) {
+		/*
+		 * With a driver reorder buffer there is no tid_rx to compare
+		 * the timeout against, so a repeated request would always be
+		 * declined. Restart the session below instead, as for a new
+		 * dialog token.
+		 */
+		if (sta->ampdu_mlme.tid_rx_token[tid] == dialog_token &&
+		    !ieee80211_hw_check(&local->hw, SUPPORTS_REORDERING_BUFFER)) {
 			struct tid_ampdu_rx *tid_rx;
 
 			ht_dbg_ratelimited(sta->sdata,
